1. Bit - The bit interacts with the transmission to transfer torque from the motor. It also has contact with the external environment as it comes into contact with the screw or bolt being tightened/loosened.
2. Transmission - The transmission interacts with the bit, motor, and housing (as it is usually housed within).
3. Motor - The motor interacts with the electrical system to receive power from the battery holder. It also interacts with the transmission to transfer torque.
4. Electrical System - The electrical system interacts with the motor and battery holder to provide power.
5. Battery Holder - The battery holder interacts with the electrical system to supply power, and it has contact with the housing as it is usually housed within.
6. Housing - The housing contains several components (transmission, motor, battery holder) so it interacts with them. It also interacts with the external environment for protection of internal parts.
7. External Environment - This refers to everything outside the screwdriver and can interact with any exposed component such as the bit or housing.

