2. Transmission - The transmission interacts with the motor, receiving power and converting it for use by the bit. It also interacts with the electrical system to control its operation.
3. Motor - The motor provides power to the transmission and is controlled by the electrical system. It may interact with the battery holder as a source of power.
4. Electrical System - The electrical system controls the motor's operation, receives input from the external environment (e.g., trigger), and interacts with the battery holder for power supply.
5. Battery Holder - The battery holder provides power to the electrical system and motor. It may interact with the housing for structural support or containment.
6. Housing - The housing contains and supports various components, including the transmission, motor, and battery holder. It interacts with the external environment as it protects internal components from damage.
7. External Environment - The external environment includes user inputs (e.g., trigger) and interactions between the bit and materials being drilled or fastened.

